.TH _PRINTF 3 "August 2026" "Holberton School" "C Library Functions"
.SH NAME
_printf \- produce output according to a format
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "main.h"
.PP
.B int _printf(const char *format, ...);
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B _printf
function produces output according to a format.

The
.I format
string is composed of zero or more directives.

The function writes its output to the standard output stream.

The following conversion specifiers are supported:
.TP
.B c
Prints a character.
.TP
.B s
Prints a string.
.TP
.B %
Prints a percent sign.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The
.B _printf
function returns the number of characters printed, excluding the terminating null byte.

If
.I format
is NULL, the function returns -1.
.SH EXAMPLES
The following example prints a string and a character:

.nf
#include "main.h"

int main(void)
{
    _printf("Hello %s%c\\n", "World", '!');
    return (0);
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR printf (3)
